umberline q:telescoping} (4) Because U ⁡ ( ℱ 0 ) U(\mathcal{F}_{0}) is fixed for a given initial filesystem, maximizing the cumulative dense reward is equivalent to maximizing the sparse objective, following potential-based reward shaping ( Ng et al., 1999 ) . Advantages are computed at each step, following multi-turn GRPO implementations ( Baronio et al., 2025 ) , thereby allowing earlier builder turns to receive a denser learning signal.
